1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,550
As many of you here today have worked in the hotel industry for some time,

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:13,100
I'm sure you have experienced the problem of high staff turnover in your hotels.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,197
Every hotel relies on having loyal

4
00:00:16,197 --> 00:00:22,390
and experienced members of staff who make sure that everything runs smoothly.

5
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:28,340
If staff are constantly changing, it can make life difficult for everyone.

6
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:34,020
But why do staff leave frequently in many hotels?

7
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:41,380
Of course, many hotel jobs, such as cleaning, are low-skilled and are not well-paid.

8
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:44,440
A lot of managers think it's this

9
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:49,160
and the long hours that are the main causes of high staff turnover -

10
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,080
but what they don't realise

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:57,680
is that it's the lack of training in many hotel jobs which is a huge factor.

12
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:03,450
So, what kind of problems does a high turnover of staff cause?

13
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:09,388
Well, having to recruit new staff all the time can be very time-consuming,

14
00:01:09,388 --> 00:01:16,240
and managers may have to cover some duties while waiting for new staff to arrive.

15
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:21,040
This means they don't have time to think about less immediate problems

16
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,720
such as how to improve their service.

17
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:30,490
When staff leave, it can also severely affect the colleagues they leave behind.

18
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:33,313
It has a negative effect on remaining staff,

19
00:01:33,313 --> 00:01:37,900
who may start to feel that they too should be thinking about leaving.

20
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:41,750
So, what can be done to change this situation?

21
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:46,940
Firstly, managers should stop making basic errors

22
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,410
which leave their staff feeling upset and resentful.

23
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:53,540
When organising shifts, for example

24
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:58,090
make sure you never give certain staff preferential treatment.

25
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:02,750
All staff should be given some choice about when they work,

26
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:07,410
and everyone should have to work some evening and weekend shifts.

27
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:10,280
If you treat staff fairly

28
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:15,830
they'll be more likely to step in and help when extra staff are needed.

29
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:21,670
Keeping staff happy has other tangible benefits for the business.

30
00:02:21,670 --> 00:02:24,850
Take the Dunwich Hotel as an example.

31
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:29,400
It had been experiencing a problem with staff complaints

32
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,677
and in order to deal with this,

33
00:02:32,677 --> 00:02:36,590
invested in staff training and improved staff conditions.

34
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:40,083
Not only did the level of complaints fall,

35
00:02:40,083 --> 00:02:47,070
but they also noticed a significant increase in the amount each customer spent during their stay.

36
00:02:47,070 --> 00:02:54,760
They have now introduced a customer loyalty scheme which is going really well.

37
00:02:54,760 --> 00:03:00,797
Now I'd like to look at some ways you can reduce staff turnover in your hotels,

38
00:03:00,797 --> 00:03:04,580
and I'll do this by giving some examples of hotels

39
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:07,190
where I've done some training recently.

40
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:10,120
The Sun Club received feedback

41
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:14,870
which showed that staff thought managers didn't value their opinions.

42
00:03:14,870 --> 00:03:17,700
They weren't made to feel they were partners

43
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:21,550
who were contributing to the success of the business as a whole.

44
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:24,460
This situation has changed.

45
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:29,600
Junior staff at all levels are regularly invited to meetings

46
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,970
where their ideas are welcomed.

47
00:03:31,970 --> 00:03:38,790
A year ago, The Portland recognised the need to invest in staff retention.

48
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:45,870
Their first step was to introduce a scheme for recognising talent amongst their employees.

49
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:49,579
The hope is that organising training for individuals

50
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:54,680
with management potential will encourage them to stay with the business.

51
00:03:54,680 --> 00:04:04,760
At Bluewater, managers decided to recognise 50 high achievers from across the company's huge hotel chain.

52
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:10,770
As a reward, they're sent on an all-expenses-paid trip abroad every year.

53
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:14,420
Fun is an important element in the trips

54
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:19,100
but there's also the opportunity to learn something useful.

55
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:22,754
This year's trip included a visit to a brewery,

56
00:04:22,754 --> 00:04:27,870
where staff learned about the new beer that would be served in the hotel.

57
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:34,970
Pentlow Hotels identified that retention of junior reception staff was an issue.

58
00:04:34,970 --> 00:04:42,783
In order to encourage them to see that working in a hotel could be worthwhile and rewarding,

59
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:46,460
with good prospects, they introduced a management programme.

60
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:49,560
These staff were given additional responsibilities

61
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:53,480
and the chance to work in various roles in the hotel.

62
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:58,730
Green Planet wanted to be seen as a caring employer.

63
00:04:58,730 --> 00:05:04,330
To make life easier for staff, many of whom had childcare responsibilities,

64
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:09,930
the hotel began issuing vouchers to help cover the cost of childcare.

65
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:13,560
Louise Marsh at The Amesbury

66
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:17,320
has one of the best staff retention rates in the business.

67
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,356
Since she joined the company,

68
00:05:19,356 --> 00:05:25,870
she has made a huge effort to achieve this by creating a co-operative and supportive environment.

69
00:05:25,870 --> 00:05:31,490
For her, the staff are part of a large family where everyone is valued.

70
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:34,000
OK, now I'd like to...
